B.P8=new A.d3("`hsv / hsva` cannot be used as `uniforms`, and hence cannot be piped in. Instead use `vec4 / vec3` or `rgba / rgb`.",null,!0,null)
B.P9=new A.d3("Although both types of `Primitives` have a child structure that represents the `Fragment`, they are essentially the same. They're supplied so for ease of reference.",null,null,null)
B.Pa=new A.d3("It is absolutely necessary that the values provided to the zIndex functions are all different (as they indicate the zIndex for each Object / Group)",null,!0,null)
B.Pd=new A.d3("It is also recommended to disable Blur from the Compositor settings in case any Shader lies below a Blurred element, as that might massively impact Performance.",null,null,null)
B.Pe=new A.d3("Window View : divided into `Fragments` that have a fixed width, `Fragment` : Houses `Bars` and `Particles`",null,null,null)
B.Pf=new A.d3("vecn needs to be supplied in with all n values. vec2(1) will not be accepted, however vec2(1, 1) will be.",null,!0,null)
B.Pg=new A.d3("No Intermediate Layers in this Group, hence no PassThrough() function",null,null,null)
B.Ph=new A.d3("You can specify a different yaml file via the `-f` CLI Argument",null,null,null)
B.Pi=new A.d3("For this reason, the `Audio-driving Shader's FPS` also determines the Audio Output variance in the subsequent chained `Shaders`",null,null,null)
B.Pj=new A.d3("`fragment.coords` in `Linear` and `Angular` automatically resolve to `r_gl_FragCoord`",null,null,null)
B.qs=new A.d3("Both Linear and Angular Visualisers have the same Life Cycle Functions",null,null,null)
B.Pk=new A.d3("The `.` selector is used for styling the underlying GL Area within the Window that displays the Shader. The `#` selector is used for styling the Window itself",null,null,null)
B.Pl=new A.d3("By default, `config.yaml` file present in `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME` is read. You can specify the name of a different `.yaml` file (also present in `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`) by specifiying the `-f` CLI Argument, followed by the file name (without the extension)",null,null,null)
B.Pn=new A.d3("You can define your own attributes that can be overriden by the config file to further fine-tune the outcomes",null,null,null)
B.Po=new A.d3("For Information about Fragments, Primitives and internal Working, refer to the Linear Visualiser Documentation",null,null,null)
B.qt=new A.d3("Avoid directly using gl_FragCoord for querying coordinates. Instead use `bar.fragment.coords`, or `particle.fragment.coords`",null,!0,null)
B.Pp=new A.d3("Use the '\\n' escape sequence to go to the next line while writing data to the pipe.",null,null,null)
B.Pq=new A.d3("numberOfIterations should be an integer value, or should be a #define variable having an integer value, either in an included file or declared previously within the same file",null,null,null)
B.Pr=new A.d3(u.D,null,null,null)
B.Ps=new A.d3("The zIndices that are passed to the functions are all relative, meaning that all the zIndices begin from 0.",null,null,null)
B.Pt=new A.d3("If you see little Audio reaction in the Visualisers while using YouTube, ensure that the `stable volume` setting on YouTube has been disabled.",null,null,null)
B.Pu=new A.d3("By default, for a `Shader` with the name `ShaderName`, the file `ShaderName.glsl` is read. This behaviour can be overriden by specifying the desired name in the `YAML Configuration file`",null,null,null)
B.Pw=new A.d3("Besides Uniforms, `gl_FragCoord` and `FragColor` are also to be specified to handle input and output values for the current Fragment Shader",null,null,null)
B.Px=new A.DJ("")
